<!--CLI Documentation — AgentsMdCommand
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.cli.documentation.AgentsMdCommand-->
<clidocumentation:AgentsMdCommand xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:clicap="org.blockml.bml.cli.capability"
  xmlns:clidocumentation="org.blockml.bml.cli.documentation"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    blockml agents-md specification
  </is>
  <documentation>
    <![CDATA[
    Syntax:
        blockml agents-md generate [--src dir]

        agents-md is a parent command. V1 defines generate only.
        The command parses flags, calls clicap:GenerateAgentsMd, and prints its lines.
        A missing or unknown subcommand prints the short USAGE and exits 2.

        Corpus: the project source folder (--src, else blockml.config.json srcDir,
        else blocks) plus blocks roots of direct dependencies and devDependencies.
        A dependency is included when package.json declares blockml.library or
        the package has blockml.config.json. Packages are resolved as
        node_modules/<name> from the project root upward. optionalDependencies
        and transitive dependencies are skipped. Library dependencies are not
        followed. This is not the validate --all corpus.

        Included blocks descend from org.blockml.bml.core.AgentInstructions and
        are not that type. sections and rules are separate streams. Each stream
        sorts by order ascending (default 1000), then FQN ascending. Children
        of one aggregation stay in document order. Every section is emitted
        before any rule.

        Every heading is level 1. The rules heading is the aggregation name
        with an initial capital (Rules). Each rule is a markdown list item.
        Output is <root>/AGENTS.md.
        At least one section or rule overwrites the file and exits 0.
        Neither → exit 1; an existing AGENTS.md is left unchanged.

    Printed help:
    Usage: blockml agents-md generate [--src dir]
           blockml agents-md --help

    When: rewrite AGENTS.md from AgentInstructions blocks.

    Searches the project source folder and the blocks roots of direct
    dependencies and devDependencies. A dependency counts when it declares
    blockml.library or has blockml.config.json. Does not follow transitive
    or optional dependencies. Does not use the validate --all corpus.

    Sorts AgentInstructions by order ascending, then FQN, once for sections
    and again for rules. Sections come first. Children of one block stay in
    document order. Every heading is level 1. Rules are a list under # Rules.

    --src dir     project source folder (default: blockml.config.json srcDir, else blocks)

    Overwrites AGENTS.md when at least one section or rule is found.
    No AgentInstructions content → exit 1; an existing AGENTS.md is left unchanged.

    Related: init, validate.
    ]]>
  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="clidocumentation:Commands" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="clidocumentation:InitCommand" relation="SeeAlso" />
    <see type="clicap:GenerateAgentsMd" relation="SeeAlso" />
  </references>
</clidocumentation:AgentsMdCommand>
